{
    "name": "8-bit DDS Waveform Generator (76 components)",
    "description": "Direct-Digital-Synthesis sawtooth generator spanning all four layers: an 8-bit PHASE ACCUMULATOR (8-bit ripple adder + clocked dff register, fed back) increments by a frequency word each clock; an 8-bit R-2R DAC converts the ramping count to an analog staircase (digital→analog bridges auto-inserted); an op-amp buffer + RC reconstruction filter smooth it. Preset frequency word = 16 → sawtooth period 16 clocks. Run a ~80µs transient and probe DAC (raw staircase) + FOUT (smoothed). (Validated on ngspice: clean 0–4.7V sawtooth, period exact.)",
    "tags": ["mixed-signal", "dds", "dac", "digital", "waveform", "flagship", "advanced"],
